WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:03.879
Unit six. Tech Ethics Basics!

2
00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:09.643
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:12.506
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.556 --> 00:00:16.456
Today we learn about Tech Ethics Basics. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.105 --> 00:00:22.063
Ethics. Say it with me. Ethics!

6
00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:30.799
Responsible use. Say it with me. Responsible use!

7
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:39.087
Consequence. Say it with me. Consequence!

8
00:00:42.551 --> 00:00:46.881
Fairness. Say it with me. Fairness!

9
00:00:50.395 --> 00:00:55.015
Privacy right. Say it with me. Privacy right!

10
00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:03.136
Digital divide. Say it with me. Digital divide!

11
00:01:06.614 --> 00:01:10.747
Access. Say it with me. Access!

12
00:01:14.244 --> 00:01:18.951
Accountability. Say it with me. Accountability!

13
00:01:22.388 --> 00:01:41.046
Tech ethics means thinking about the responsible use of technology and its consequence. Fairness includes protecting a privacy right and understanding the digital divide, since not everyone has equal access. Accountability means taking responsibility for how I use technology.

14
00:01:41.096 --> 00:01:44.459
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:50.652
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:50.702 --> 00:01:52.029
Consequence!

17
00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:58.544
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:58.594 --> 00:01:59.744
Access!

19
00:02:00.998 --> 00:02:12.002
Did you know? Around the world, millions of people still don't have reliable internet access, which can limit their opportunities to learn and work online!

20
00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:14.530
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:15.576 --> 00:02:26.379
Think and answer. What does 'the digital divide' mean, and why is it a fairness issue?

22
00:02:26.429 --> 00:02:27.702
Great answer!

23
00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:34.151
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
